From: lateautumn233 <lateautumn233@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] k27: a realtime computation past the maximum is held to
 it rather than refused

The board's timer runs at 19.2 MHz, where max_rt_quantum (50 ms) is 960000 ticks. coreaudiod asks for its I/O thread
THREAD_TIME_CONSTRAINT_POLICY with a computation of 1200000 ticks (50 ms at Apple's 24 MHz; period 1536000):
thread_policy_set refused it, every I/O thread stayed non-realtime ("Failed to change thread to realtime priority"),
the HAL's clock never moved and WebKit's players stopped at their first second. The computation is held to the
maximum when the constraint allows it, as a computation below half the constraint is already raised.

(not yet committed on branch k27: exported from the worktree's diff)
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/thread_policy.c b/osfmk/kern/thread_policy.c
index bb1f51b..cf36182 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/thread_policy.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/thread_policy.c
@@ -405,6 +405,15 @@ thread_policy_set_internal(
 		info = (thread_time_constraint_with_priority_policy_t)policy_info;
 
 
+		/*
+		 * A computation past the maximum is held to it rather than refused: the board's timer runs at 19.2 MHz,
+		 * where 50 ms is 960000 ticks, and coreaudiod asks for its I/O thread a computation of 1200000 ticks (50 ms
+		 * at Apple's 24 MHz), so every I/O thread it starts stays non-realtime and the HAL's clock never moves.
+		 */
+		if (info->computation > max_rt_quantum && info->constraint >= max_rt_quantum) {
+			info->computation = max_rt_quantum;
+		}
+
 		if (info->constraint < info->computation ||
 		    info->computation > max_rt_quantum ||
 		    info->computation < min_rt_quantum) {
